  - name: Longmont scenario model, Feb 2023 update
    authority: City of Longmont (scenario workbook created by Nick Russell)
    url:
    description: 'The scenario model behind the first Paths model. It is the origin
      of most action trajectories (fuel switching, vehicle incentives, waste diversion,
      last-mile connections, renewables), the building floor areas and energy-use-intensity
      improvements, the registered EVs, the vehicle miles per vehicle and the electricity
      and gas use by utility. Sent by Francie Jaffe (City of Longmont); the date is
      when the file was last saved, which approximates when Kausal received it. This
      file is byte-identical to client/Longmont_Model_Feb 2023_Update_FINAL(2).xlsx.
      Years covered: 2016-2050.; Attachment: client/Longmont (CO) Client/KP material/Longmont_Model_Feb
      2023_Update_FINAL.xlsx; Format: .xlsx; Geographic Coverage: City of Longmont,
      Colorado; Date Last Updated: 2023-09-12; Updated by: Jouni Tuomisto (register
      row drafted by Claude, 2026-11-21)'
    edition:
    target: data_point
  dataset:
    forecast_from: 2025
    time_resolution: yearly
    is_editable: true
  index_columns:
  - emission_sectors
  - Year
  updated_at: '1795523311'
  units:
